*.swp

# Aegis runtime
aegis-sandbox-audit.jsonl
*.jsonl.tmp

# Secrets (defense in depth)
.env
.env.local
.pypirc
.npmrc

# Internal sprint / audit artifacts — never publish to the public repo.
# These hold ops-internal review evidence (exposure audits, cross-review logs)
# that reference private substrate paths. Kept local-only.
#
# **Anchored to the repo root (S053).** Without the leading slash this pattern
# matches a `deploy/` at ANY depth, so a customer-facing deployment unit written
# to `docs/deploy/` disappeared silently — the file was created, `git add`
# refused it, and nothing said why unless someone looked. The intent was always
# this one top-level scratch directory.
/deploy/
